"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. It was introduced by Alex with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The project has since seen several developments: the budget was increased to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration; strategic partnerships with TechInnovate for AI research were established; and the team expanded with Mike Chen and Lisa Ray joining for their expertise in machine learning and cloud computing. A call for ideas was issued to R&D to leverage AI for data visualization, with proposals due by July 20th. Training programs for the coding team and project managers were approved with a $15,000 budget. The project reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with a successfully tested prototype for secure file sharing, and the next phase involving user interface enhancements is planned for October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought from stakeholders by the end of November."
